1[1]. The issuance of a restraining order as a temporary measure by an authorized police officer to ensure the protection of the victim and the restriction of certain actions of the abuser is mandatory in cases of initiation or ongoing investigation under Articles 108, 109, 115, 117, 118, 120, 126, 137 and 138, Article 143, Part 3, subparagraph "e" and Part 4, Article 144, Part 2, subparagraph "i" and Part 3, Articles 144[1]–144[3] and 151, Article 160, Part 2, subparagraph "a" and Part 3, and Article 381[1] of the Criminal Code of Georgia.

